<title>UK: Marks &amp; Spencer first half profit up 11.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Marks &amp; Spencer first half profit up 11.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>26 weeks to September 28</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		 10.4		vs     9.3</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	   3.3		vs     3.0</p>
<p> Pretax		     430.1		vs   385.4</p>
<p> Turnover		 3,532.2		vs 3,248.2</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 420.1 to 465.0 million stg.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 401.8		  vs 362.1</p>
<p> Interest income	   29.7		  vs  25.0</p>
<p> Tax			  137.6		  vs 124.5</p>
<p> Net taxed		  292.5		  vs 260.9</p>
<p> Attributable	     292.5		  vs 260.9</p>
<p> Pay date		   January 17 1997</p>
<p>Div registration date  November 19  Ex-div date		November 11</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
